This plugin is adapted from the Telegram channel plugin in
anthropics/claude-plugins-official (https://github.com/anthropics/claude-plugins-official),
path external_plugins/telegram, version 0.0.7, commit
1e96c6b0a0f06cad576086243f3d06397c4ddf44, licensed under the Apache License,
Version 2.0. The license text is in LICENSE.

Changes from that version are listed in UPSTREAM.md, and each modified source
file says it was modified in its header comment.

Patterns adapted, in this plugin's own code, from MIT-licensed projects:
- op7418/Claude-to-IM-skill (src/permission-gateway.ts): a map of pending
  permission asks that fails closed on a timer, on abort and on shutdown
  (server.ts, askButton).
- nanocoai/nanoclaw (container/agent-runner/src/poll-loop.ts,
  src/providers/claude.ts, src/modules/scheduling/create.ts): session rotation
  by age and size, the stale-resume pattern, systemPrompt snapshot off, and a
  daily cap on unattended runs (agent.ts).
No code was copied from them.

Login: the documented login is a token from `claude setup-token`, each person
with their own Claude account; an ANTHROPIC_API_KEY works as an alternative.
Anthropic's Agent SDK overview says: "Unless previously approved, Anthropic
does not allow third party developers to offer claude.ai login or rate limits
for their products, including agents built on the Claude Agent SDK." Whoever
installs this plugin decides how that applies to them (README.md, "Login").
